{
 "id": "2016-schirpke-alpine",
 "name": "Alpine Landscape Liking (rating)",
 "description": "Faithful replication of the photo questionnaire \"Landscape in the Alps: Which landscape do you like?\" from Schirpke, Timmermann, Tappeiner & Tasser (2016), Cultural ecosystem services of mountain regions: Modelling the aesthetic value, Ecological Indicators 69:78-90. Participants rate 24 panoramic photographs of Alpine landscapes in Tyrol and South Tyrol (alpine pastures, timberline, forests, meadows, orchards, villages, rivers, scree slopes), four per page in the original fixed order, from 1 (I don't like it at all) to 10 (I like it very much), then answer six personal questions (gender, tourist or not, city or village, settlement size, nationality, age group). In the original study 967 people were surveyed in the Stubai, Lech and Puster valleys, Vinschgau and Bozen; the published mean rating of every picture (Table 2, from 4.29 for a village to 8.26 for steep meadows with a lake) is embedded in the page for comparison. Ratings are keyed by picture number (P01-P24). Photographs and questionnaire wording come from the supplementary questionnaire of the author manuscript (Europe PMC PMC4962904, CC BY-NC-ND), used unmodified with credit to the authors; the template will be removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) a web survey instead of an on-site paper questionnaire; (2) English only, the original was in German and Italian; (3) panoramas are shown at screen width, so they appear smaller on phones than on the printed sheet; (4) a consent question is added at the start.",
